format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANABE TAKAYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO MANABU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIKAWA HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>BOUET, LAURENCE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DESPAX, CORINE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FURUYA, AKINORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHKUBO, TOSHIFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ROUSSET, ABEL</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAILHADES, PHILIPPE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANABE, TAKAYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, MANABU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIKAWA, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An opto-magnetic recording medium such as an optical disk or an optical card and its manufacturing method, and an opto-magnetic recording/reproducing device for recording/reproducing information on/from an opto-magnetic recording medium. The opto-magnetic recording medium has recording and reflecting layers on a substrate. The recording layer has a layered structure of at least one spinel ferrite (or rutile oxide or hematite) layer and at least one garnet ferrite layer. The layered structure is preferably formed on a track where information is to be recorded. A method of manufacturing such an opto-magnetic recording medium comprises a step of heating the medium at 500  DEG C to 700  DEG C, preferably at 600  DEG C to 630  DEG C after the recording medium is formed. The opto-magnetic information recording/reproducing device is preferably used for such an opto-magnetic recording medium because the wavelength of the light for write is different from that of the light for read.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Support d'enregistrement opto-magnétique, tel qu'un disque optique ou une carte optique et son procédé de fabrication; dispositif opto-magnétique servant à enregistrer sur un support d'enregistrement opto-magnétique et à reproduire des informations depuis ledit support. Ce dernier possède des couches d'enregistrement et de réflexion situées sur un substrat. La couche d'enregistrement présente une structure stratifiée composée d'au moins d'une couche de ferrite de spinelle (ou oxyde de rutile ou hématite) et d'au moins une couche de ferrite de grenat. Cette structure stratifiée se trouve, de préférence, sur une piste sur laquelle les informations doivent être enregistrées. L'invention se rapporte également à un procédé de fabrication d'un tel support d'enregistrement opto-magnétique, qui consiste à chauffer le support à une température comprise entre 500  DEG C et 700  DEG C, de préférence entre 600  DEG C et 630  DEG C, après la formation du support d'enregistrement. On utilise, de préférence, le dispositif opto-magnétique d'enregistrement et de reproduction d'informations pour ce support d'enregistrement opto-magnétique, étant donné que la longueur d'onde de la lumière d'écriture est différente de celle de la lumière de lecture.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>